<title>NEW ZEALAND: Telecom NZ says has resumed share buyback.</title>
<headline>Telecom NZ says has resumed share buyback.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Telecom Corp of New Zealand said on Monday it had resumed its NZ$1 billion share buyback scheme on Friday.</p>
<p>It said on Friday it bought 1.95 million shares at $6.65-6.66 on market.</p>
<p>In the first stage of buyback, which ended before last week's profit result, Telecom purchased 55 million shares at a cost of $350 million.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
